# Playtest policy

Killmarket is a **visual video game**. The human evaluates playability, feel, and visuals first.

## Do (without being asked)

- Verify **code quality** (consistency, correctness, focused diffs)
- Verify **builds** (`npm run build`) when changes could break the pipeline
- Prefer small, reviewable changes that match existing patterns

## Do not (unless the human explicitly asks)

- Open the app in a browser / IDE browser to “try it”
- Drive UI clicks, deploy drones, fire missions, or other in-game flows to QA
- Screenshot or screen-record gameplay to judge look/feel
- Spend time on playability judgment (“feels good”, “arc looks right on map”)

## When reporting done

- Summarize what changed and how to try it
- Leave playtesting to the human; only run interactive product tests when asked
